# L0 (the dry run of the graft build, cardm, no device): optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/build_k64j_lo.sh with LO_BUILD_DRY_RUN=1. It reads the checkout, the base graft (~/opgraft-K64j: the
# K64j binary the serving images bake) and the saved factory bases, checks every recorded sha (the vendored stock all-gather factory, ag_link_offset.patch, the patched factory, K64j's sources
# and kernels, the base binary against scripts/ci/packed_any_admission.py's K64J_TTNNCPP_SHA256), prints every docker, cp, mv and generator command it WOULD run and runs none of them.
# It opens no card; the cardm step only names card M as context. READ: the console ends '### dry run: nothing built' with no FAIL line. STOP otherwise (a FAIL line names what differs).
# Duration (estimate): 3 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the separate-links run of the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own
# image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/build_k64j_lo.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=LO_BUILD_DRY_RUN=1
